    "body": "Diving in my mail archives.\r\n\r\n## Log\r\n\r\n### September 2011\r\n\r\n* [Implement CSS Mask Image properties (mask, mask-image, etc.)](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=686281)\r\n   It's when `mask-composite` was added to Firefox, 10 years ago.\r\n\r\n### January 2016\r\n\r\n* Compat. [Spec -webkit-mask-*](https://github.com/whatwg/compat/issues/14#issuecomment-177340371)\r\n* Mozilla. [Add webkit-prefixed aliases for CSS Mask Image properties (\"-webkit-mask-image\" and associated properties)](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1242617)\r\n* Mozilla. [Add -webkit- prefixed aliases for mask-border-* properties](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1244492) Still open.\r\n\r\n### February 2016\r\n* Mozilla. [Update WebKit aliases for CSS mask properties](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1245997)\r\n    Here @miketaylr (moz) dropped some of the values, but composite was kept as-is\r\n\r\n\r\n### October 2016\r\n\r\n* Mozilla. [Content with -webkit-mask-size but not -webkit-mask-repeat is clipped in Firefox, not Safari](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1308963)  \r\n    The comments have their share of information\r\n* Mozilla [Handle -webkit-mask-repeat default value compatibility issue](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1310135)\r\n* CSS Spec. [[css-masking] initial value of mask-repeat and mask-position](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/599)\r\n\r\n> Blink implemented the no-repeat (-webkit-)mask-repeat default value in https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=628968, but it was reverted according to comment 11 of that bug due to https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=645000. in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1305697#c5\r\n\r\n## Unrelated \r\n* [mask-image and SVG on input element fails in Firefox, Safari, and Edge, works in Chrome](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1501480)\r\n\r\n\r\n🚨  The important thing probably is that most of the webcompat issues I could browse, find about `mask` **were NOT about mask-composite**.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
